        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "SU(3)_C x SU(2)_L x U(1)_Y (x U(1)_X) as a symmetry of division algebraic ladder operators",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Furey, C."
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20180511",
      "bibo:doi": "10.1140/epjc/s10052-018-5844-7",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://doi.org/10.1140/epjc/s10052-018-5844-7",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We demonstrate a model which captures certain attractive features of SU(5) theory, while providing a pos- sible escape from proton decay. In this paper we show how ladder operators arise from the division algebras R, C, H, and O. From the SU(n) symmetry of these ladder operators, we then demonstrate a model which has much structural sim- ilarity to Georgi and Glashow’s SU(5) grand uniﬁed theory. However, in this case, the transitions leading to proton decay are expected to be blocked, given that they coincide with presumably forbidden transformations which would incor- rectly mix distinct algebraic actions. As a result, we ﬁnd that we are left with Gsm = SU(3)C × SU(2)L × U(1)Y /Z6. Finally, we point out that if U(n) ladder symmetries are used in place of SU(n), it may then be possible to ﬁnd this same Gsm = SU(3)C × SU(2)L × U(1)Y /Z6, together with an extra U(1)X symmetry, related to B−L.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/furey-2018-epjc-78-375/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/furey-2018-epjc-78-375"
    }
  ]
}
